                <pb facs="0819" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672/328: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Comissioner in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-12-12T20:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                                1924—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 13—6:53
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>232. Minister of Foreign Affairs intimated informally day before yesterday to
                    delegate at Angora that our treaties would not be presented to Assembly for
                    ratification until our Senate had ratified or at least seemed to be on the point
                    of ratifying them. It would be most helpful if I could have exact present status
                    of treaties before Senate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
